<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:39Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>What have the talks with Russia and the US in Abu Dhabi achieved for Ukraine?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:64b0e7ddb75e8ddbc97982a31c429e4d7bdce7f1de8f73b082803eb4d4bbed02</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T16:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-have-the-talks-with-russia-and-the-us-in-abu-dhabi-achieved-for-ukraine/a-79930613--89b8a9b8f641.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-have-the-talks-with-russia-and-the-us-in-abu-dhabi-achieved-for-ukraine/a-79930613?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The first trilateral talks between Ukraine, the US and Russia in nine months have ended with an agreement on exchanging prisoners. Does this mark a genuine breakthrough and a step toward peace?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Hungary eases abortion rules</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8cf46bc9d8e342fd5f32b21658aad8ff2fa62f0be2c092903c1b973da6ec10a9</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T16:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hungary-eases-abortion-rules/a-79931614--3bb42fe8feff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hungary-eases-abortion-rules/a-79931614?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The reforms mark a break the the conservative policies of former PM Viktor Orban. The controversial "heartbeat regulation" is to be scrapped and women are to be better protected against violence.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Sri Lanka: Rights groups sound alarm over proposed anti-terror law</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:30a8bc7236a5534c606594caa1e29e8c71b24c2065536eb18850414d0ce23f02</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/sri-lanka-rights-groups-sound-alarm-over-proposed-anti-terror-law/a-79932227--abd4d2b11674.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/sri-lanka-rights-groups-sound-alarm-over-proposed-anti-terror-law/a-79932227?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Sri Lankan government is looking to replace a controversial anti-terror law but critics say the new one is just as bad.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>UK court convicts 2 Iranian men of spying on journalists</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3396046f7799983df8595bcc1b3421ce8e464a8948e829898a2f08aa19e496a2</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-court-convicts-2-iranian-men-of-spying-on-journalists/a-79931583--9da85f420d5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-court-convicts-2-iranian-men-of-spying-on-journalists/a-79931583?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A London court has found two Iranian citizens guilty of surveilling reporters for a Persian-language television station critical of Iran's government. One was also convicted of planning a violent attack against them.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Jensen Huang: Spy row, second affair leaves Nvidia without its rockstar CEO</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c5a8f67e72d43fd27ca3ddb391c0b82394e3eadcadd0610fd509d1ccacbf4e6f</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/jensen-huang-spy-row-second-affair-leaves-nvidia-without-its-rockstar-ceo/a-79926972--471686cc8872.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jensen-huang-spy-row-second-affair-leaves-nvidia-without-its-rockstar-ceo/a-79926972?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jensen Huang, who built Nvidia into the world’s dominant AI chipmaker, is stepping down as CEO after a second affair came to light. DW examines how losing its figurehead will affect the firm and the US-China AI race.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Iran: Exiled journalists still repressed by regime</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cff57f812547b827d5730ce2dd9a3a915d3f75251071b5602278f6f8b548cc8b</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:30Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T14:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-exiled-journalists-still-repressed-by-regime/a-79929694--82c71d3aa718.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-exiled-journalists-still-repressed-by-regime/a-79929694?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For many independent reporters, leaving Iran does not mean fully escaping the grasp of the Iranian state. The regime uses family members, bank accounts and the property they left behind to apply pressure across borders.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>China's Xi Jinping renews calls for 'reunification' with Taiwan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9f5030ac0c9fc0f177e3598b931c4417f81028bf7ac4c238ad123449812111e2</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:33Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T13:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-s-xi-jinping-renews-calls-for-reunification-with-taiwan/a-79929738--c3c1f561b896.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-s-xi-jinping-renews-calls-for-reunification-with-taiwan/a-79929738?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Xi Jinping said that reunification was inevitable, but stopped short of mentioning military force. Taiwan though swiftly rejected Beijing's demands as tensions continue over the island's future.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Israel strikes Gaza hospital, says Hamas senior figure inside</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:67673a2b65fa5dab21663b32132dbeaaa50ccfb58fbe68b9743bce685a712604</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T11:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/israel-strikes-gaza-hospital-says-hamas-senior-figure-inside/a-79927645--35a0867b6650.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/israel-strikes-gaza-hospital-says-hamas-senior-figure-inside/a-79927645?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Israel says Hamas was using the hospital as a military command center, while Palestinian officials report at least six people killed, including a surgeon. The strike comes amid an increasingly fragile ceasefire.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil electoral court fines Meta, sees no deliberate election bias</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2dbc6bf074f1eb63bf172def6cb25eec1222b5c47d86875317ec0743d994e73d</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brazil-electoral-court-fines-meta-sees-no-deliberate-election-bias/a-79920780--215a8f08f312.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brazil-electoral-court-fines-meta-sees-no-deliberate-election-bias/a-79920780?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The fine came after President Lula's coalition filed a complaint. The court said there was no evidence of intent to influence the election. Meta said it will defend itself against "false allegations."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Is AIIB's complaint mechanism failing affected communities?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5c221bb687a1615c84ec9a97aa179c322bb988b46472060968320ba5ae7b2644</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-aiib-s-complaint-mechanism-failing-affected-communities/a-79919917--1bfa788b7764.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-aiib-s-complaint-mechanism-failing-affected-communities/a-79919917?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank has a grievance redress mechanism for people affected by projects it finances. But those seeking to file a complaint face significant hurdles. Critics say reforms are needed.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Wael Mohya could make German football history at 17</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f5a2fc05c3713045bfbeb92819c9e3462af25fb35f6ff15d963502a56212003d</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787--677b2c671ea6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At just 17, Gladbach forward Wael Mohya has earned his first Germany call-up. The dual-national talent has chosen the DFB path for now — and could soon make modern national-team history.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Tundu Lissu: After escaping the death penalty, what does his guilty verdict mean for Tanzania's democracy?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f8f9614bd18581470651fc752d013d2919647ec43a944c2a9614bbc78a5c303</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T13:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tundu-lissu-after-escaping-the-death-penalty-what-does-his-guilty-verdict-mean-for-tanzania-s-democr/a-79908512--3044020567d7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tundu-lissu-after-escaping-the-death-penalty-what-does-his-guilty-verdict-mean-for-tanzania-s-democracy/a-79908512?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A treason trial could have meant death by hanging for Tanzanian opposition leader Tundu Lissu. Instead, he now faces four years in prison for incitement to unrest. Can voices of dissident truly be heard in the country?</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
